  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Daniel Ferreira (pt-0015), contrast CT on Mon 10/26 at 9:00, prepared under RBC-RAD-07:\n- Placed the order for CT abdomen and pelvis with IV contrast (sr-t0001) and linked it to the booked appointment appt-00001.\n- Contrast allergy: The radiology report written the day of his 2019 iohexol reaction rates it moderate: hives and eyelid swelling, no breathing or airway problems, blood pressure normal. His allergy list also says \"anaphylaxis.\" He added that himself in 2021 and no records were checked. Per §1 the day-of report sets the grade, so §2 premedication applies, not §3 (no contrast, call the radiologist). His shellfish and povidone-iodine allergies are not risk factors.\n- Premedication ordered: prednisone 50 mg by mouth at 20:00 on 10/25 and at 02:00 and 08:00 on 10/26 (mr-t0003). Diphenhydramine 50 mg by mouth at 08:00 on 10/26 (mr-t0004). He needs a driver.\n- Kidney function: His 9/24 creatinine is 32 days before the scan, so it is too old. His ED creatinines from 10/16–17 were taken during acute kidney injury from dehydration (1.94, then 1.46 at discharge, still above his usual ~1.0), so they don't count. Ordered a new creatinine to be drawn before the scan, between now and 08:30 on 10/26 (sr-t0002). The scan stays as booked, and the radiologist will review the result that day.\n- Metformin: Because of the kidney injury, I put metformin 1000 mg twice daily (mr-00189) on hold starting now. It stays off through at least 48 hours after the scan. Ordered a repeat creatinine for 10/28–10/30 (sr-t0006), which also covers the 1-week kidney check the ED asked for. Created task-t0007 for Dr. Okafor (due 10/30): restart metformin only if kidney function is back to normal.\n- Sent the patient an urgent portal message (comm-t0008) covering the blood draw, the premedication times, no driving and the need for a driver, stopping metformin and not restarting it himself, drinking fluids, telling CT staff about his past reaction, and when to call 911.\n- Wrote a progress note (doc-t0009) citing RBC-RAD-07.\n- I left the allergy list entry as it is. The note explains why the reaction was graded moderate.",
